// OpenCode Collab — Zed tasks.
//
// Copy this into your global tasks (`zed: open tasks`) or a project `.zed/tasks.json`.
// The session picker is a task because a language server cannot render a list picker;
// it runs in Zed's integrated terminal, lists OpenCode sessions for the current
// worktree, and pins the one you choose (sends from this worktree then target it).
//
// Adjust the absolute path below to wherever you installed this repo.
//
// NOTE: the command deliberately does NOT reference $ZED_WORKTREE_ROOT. Zed hides a task
// whenever a variable it references can't be resolved in the active context (terminal,
// project panel, non-worktree buffer), which makes the task appear only intermittently.
// Keeping it variable-free makes it always available; the CLI derives the worktree from
// Zed's injected ZED_WORKTREE_ROOT env var, falling back to the task's cwd (project root).
[
  {
    "label": "OpenCode: switch session",
    "command": "node /Users/anirudh/workspace/zed-opencode/lsp/dist/cli.js pick",
    "use_new_terminal": false,
    "allow_concurrent_runs": false,
    "reveal": "always",
    "hide": "on_success"
  }
]
